#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""One usage table across every coding harness: Kiro, l3m, Claude Code, Codex, ...

Each harness records something different, and no one source reads them all:

  * ccusage reads REAL token counts from Claude Code / Codex / opencode logs and
    prices them at published per-model list rates it pulls from LiteLLM
    (`model_prices_and_context_window.json`, models.dev fallback, embedded
    snapshot offline). Token counts are ground truth; the rate is the provider's
    list price. But ccusage prices any model LiteLLM has never heard of at
    *exactly $0* -- silently. On this machine that zeroes `claude-opus-5`, the
    single largest consumer (23B tokens -> $0.00).

  * l3m (~/CodebaseQUENNV/.../l3m) hardcodes the same published Bedrock/Anthropic
    list prices as a dated, Lean-proof-pinned snapshot (cents/1M, split
    in/out/cache-read/cache-write). Narrower than LiteLLM but it COVERS the
    frontier models LiteLLM misses -- opus-5 included. Same source (published
    list price), curated instead of fetched.

  * Kiro exposes no tokens at all -- only credits, which it writes per turn to
    its own session log. The $/credit applied to them is derived
    (credits->tokens->dollars, calibrate.py and FINDINGS.md), anchored to those
    same published prices, and carries a wide -13%/+88% band because the token
    count and the input/output mix are unmeasured.

So the trustworthy quantity is always (real tokens) x (published list price).
For Claude/Codex the tokens are logged, so cost is near-exact IF the price table
has the model. LiteLLM has the breadth; l3m has this box's frontier models.
Hence the default `--rates l3m`: l3m prices the Claude-family models it lists
(this is what recovers opus-5), LiteLLM prices everything else. `--rates litellm`
is pure ccusage, which reproduces the $0-opus-5 undercount -- kept so the gap is
visible, not hidden.

Kiro is the one harness with no token ground truth, so its column is credits and
its dollar figure is the only true *estimate* here -- the -13%/+88% band rides on
the Kiro subtotal alone; token costs are shown as points. Its rows come from
`~/.kiro/sessions/<workspace>/sess_<uuid>/messages.jsonl`, where each completed
turn appends a `usage_summary` record carrying that turn's credits; the model is
joined on from the `assistant` records sharing the turn's `executionId`, so a
session that switched models still attributes per turn.

l3m appears here twice, in two unrelated roles: as the price TABLE above, and --
since it burns Bedrock tokens of its own -- as a harness in its own right.
ccusage cannot see it (l3m keeps no Claude-Code-shaped log), so its rows are read
straight out of l3m's own bookkeeping: every turn boundary publishes the session
sidecar (`last_state.json` -- cumulative `cents` plus per-wire token counters) to
`refs/agents/state/<agent>/self` in the hub, so that ref's commit history is a
dated series of running totals, and differencing consecutive samples gives daily
usage. Cost comes from l3m's own `cents`, not from re-pricing here: l3m charges
each call at the model that call actually used, which the flattened per-wire
counters can no longer tell us. So `--rates` does not move the l3m rows, and the
`Model` cell is the session's brain -- a `consult_model` side call to a different
model folds into its parent's row.

One l3m row can carry no date (`-`): the earliest sample in a ref's history is a
conversation that was already running, so that much spend is real but the days it
happened on were never recorded. It is carried undated rather than dumped on the
day it first became visible, and it survives `--since`/`--until` like any undated
row -- dropping it would silently shrink the total.

Columns: Date | Harness | Model | Consumed | Unit | Rate | Cost (USD), where
Consumed x Rate = Cost on every row. `Unit` is `credits` for Kiro (metered) and
`Mtok` (millions of tokens) for the token-logged harnesses -- the two are not
commensurable, so `Consumed` sums only within a harness; `Cost (USD)` is the one
column comparable and summable across all of them. Token `Rate` is the effective
blended $/Mtok (cache-read pulls it below the input list price).

Usage:
  ccusage-all                     # unified daily table, l3m rates, Kiro estimated
  ccusage-all --rates litellm     # price everything the way ccusage does
  ccusage-all --credit-rate .056  # output-heavy end of the Kiro estimate
  ccusage-all --since 2026-08-01 --until 2026-08-14
  ccusage-all --json              # machine-readable rows + totals
  ccusage-all --online            # let ccusage refresh LiteLLM prices (network)
"""

import argparse
import collections
import json
import os
import pathlib
import subprocess
import sys

KIRO_SESSIONS = pathlib.Path(os.environ.get("KIRO_HOME", "~/.kiro")).expanduser() / "sessions"

# l3m-as-a-harness. The hub is a bare repo holding one state ref per agent; the
# sidecar under it is the session's running cost/usage record.
L3M_HOME = pathlib.Path("~/.l3m").expanduser()
L3M_STATE_REFS = "refs/agents/state/"
L3M_SIDECAR = "last_state.json"

# USD per Kiro credit (default) and the asymmetric band multipliers printed
# beside the Kiro subtotal. Derived, not guessed: calibrate.py re-derives both
# from local Kiro data, and FINDINGS.md carries the argument.
USD_PER_CREDIT = 0.0747
KIRO_BAND = (0.0647 / 0.0747, 0.1405 / 0.0747)

# l3m's model price table, transcribed from
# src/LlmProvider/Defs/Registry.lean (rates snapshot 2026-07-23), cents per 1M
# tokens, with the four Bedrock/Anthropic cache tiers. Keyed by a canonicalised
# model name (region/geo/provider prefixes stripped). Only the Claude family is
# re-priced from l3m: l3m lists the GPT models too, but its mantle price shape
# has no cache-read tier while ccusage reports cache-read for GPT separately, so
# re-pricing GPT from l3m would misprice cached input. LiteLLM covers the GPT
# models seen here, so l3m mode defers all non-Claude models to LiteLLM.
L3M_CLAUDE = {
    # canonical prefix          (in,   out,  cacheRead, cacheWrite)
    "claude-opus-4-8":          (500,  2500, 50,  625),
    "claude-sonnet-4-6":        (300,  1500, 30,  375),
    "claude-haiku-4-5":         (100,  500,  10,  125),
    "claude-fable-5":           (1000, 5000, 100, 1250),
    "claude-opus-5":            (500,  2500, 50,  625),   # PROVISIONAL (borrowed opus-4.8)
}

# l3m's short model aliases, from the same table, needed for the l3m HARNESS
# rows: a session that names no `--model` runs on the configured default, which
# is normally written as one of these. A leading `a/` (direct Anthropic instead
# of Bedrock) is stripped before lookup -- same model, different transport.
L3M_ALIASES = {
    "opus":   "claude-opus-4-8",
    "sonnet": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
    "haiku":  "claude-haiku-4-5",
    "fable":  "claude-fable-5",
    "gpt":    "gpt-5.6-sol",
}


def canon(model):
    """Reduce a ccusage model name to an l3m-comparable key.

    ccusage keeps a provider prefix on some names (`openai.gpt-5.6-sol`) and a
    region/geo prefix on others is already stripped (`claude-opus-4-8`), while
    l3m ids carry `us.anthropic.` / `global.anthropic.` / `openai.`. Strip all of
    them so the cores line up, and drop a trailing dated/versioned snapshot
    (`claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0`) down to the family key.
    """
    key = (model or "").lower()
    for prefix in ("us.", "eu.", "apac.", "global.", "anthropic.", "openai."):
        while key.startswith(prefix):
            key = key[len(prefix):]
    return key


def l3m_claude_rates(model):
    """The l3m Claude rate tuple for a model name, or None if l3m doesn't list it.

    Exact canonical match first, then longest-prefix (so the haiku snapshot id
    resolves to `claude-haiku-4-5`)."""
    key = canon(model)
    if key in L3M_CLAUDE:
        return L3M_CLAUDE[key]
    for name in sorted(L3M_CLAUDE, key=len, reverse=True):
        if key.startswith(name):
            return L3M_CLAUDE[name]
    return None


def l3m_cost_usd(rates, tokens):
    """l3m costCents on Bedrock/Anthropic usage -> USD. Mirrors the Lean
    `costCents` exactly, including its round-to-nearest-cent (+500000)//1e6."""
    in_c, out_c, cr_c, cw_c = rates
    cents = (
        tokens.get("inputTokens", 0) * in_c
        + tokens.get("outputTokens", 0) * out_c
        + tokens.get("cacheReadTokens", 0) * cr_c
        + tokens.get("cacheCreationTokens", 0) * cw_c
        + 500000
    ) // 1000000
    return cents / 100.0


def kiro_turns(session_dir):
    """Yield (timestamp, execution_id, credits, model) per completed Kiro turn.

    Credits arrive on a `usage_summary` record, but the model that spent them is
    only named on the `assistant` records sharing its `executionId` -- so collect
    both in one pass and join at the end."""
    messages = session_dir / "messages.jsonl"
    if not messages.is_file():
        return
    models, summaries = {}, []
    with messages.open() as handle:
        for line in handle:
            try:
                record = json.loads(line)
            except json.JSONDecodeError:
                continue
            payload = record.get("payload") or {}
            execution_id = payload.get("executionId") or record.get("id")

            if payload.get("type") == "assistant" and payload.get("reasoningModelId"):
                # Namespaced as "qdev::claude-opus-5"; keep the bare model name.
                models.setdefault(execution_id,
                                  payload["reasoningModelId"].rpartition("::")[2])
                continue

            if payload.get("type") != "usage_summary":
                continue
            credits = sum(
                summary.get("usage", 0)
                for summary in payload.get("promptTurnSummaries") or []
                if str(summary.get("unit", "")).lower().startswith("credit")
            )
            if credits > 0:
                summaries.append((record.get("timestamp"), execution_id, credits))

    for timestamp, execution_id, credits in summaries:
        yield timestamp, execution_id, credits, models.get(execution_id)


def kiro_rows(credit_rate):
    """Per (day, model) Kiro credits, read straight from Kiro's session logs.

    Credits are what Kiro records, so the dollar figure is derived here at the
    rate in force. Turns key on `executionId`, which is stable across re-reads,
    so a turn recorded twice counts once."""
    days = collections.defaultdict(lambda: collections.defaultdict(float))
    seen = set()
    for session_dir in sorted(KIRO_SESSIONS.glob("*/sess_*")):
        try:
            meta = json.loads((session_dir / "session.json").read_text())
        except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError):
            meta = {}
        # session.json names one model for the whole session, which is wrong for
        # a session that switched models; the per-turn join wins where it
        # succeeded, and this is only the fallback.
        session_model = meta.get("modelId") or "kiro-unknown"
        for timestamp, execution_id, credits, model in kiro_turns(session_dir):
            day = (timestamp or "")[:10]
            if not day or not execution_id or execution_id in seen:
                continue
            seen.add(execution_id)
            days[day][model or session_model] += credits
    rows = []
    for day, models in days.items():
        for model, credits in models.items():
            rows.append({
                "day": day, "harness": "kiro", "model": model,
                "consumed": credits, "unit": "credits", "rate": credit_rate,
                "cost": credits * credit_rate, "tokens": None,
                "priced_by": "kiro-credit",
            })
    return rows


def l3m_settings():
    """`~/.l3m/settings.json`, or `{}` if it is absent or unreadable."""
    try:
        return json.loads((L3M_HOME / "settings.json").read_text())
    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError):
        return {}


def l3m_hub_path(settings):
    """Where l3m's hub lives: `$L3M_HUB`, else settings `hub.path`, else the
    default `~/.l3m/hub.git` (L3m/Runtime/HubBoot.lean)."""
    configured = os.environ.get("L3M_HUB") or (settings.get("hub") or {}).get("path")
    return pathlib.Path(configured).expanduser() if configured else L3M_HOME / "hub.git"


def l3m_model(state, default_model):
    """The session's brain: the `--model=` it was started with, else the
    configured default (settings `llm.model`; `None` when that is unset too, and
    l3m's own built-in default -- unknowable from out here -- applies).

    Attribution is per SESSION, not per call: the sidecar's counters are keyed by
    wire (Anthropic / Bedrock Converse / Mantle), not by model, so a
    `consult_model` side call to another model folds into its parent's row. Only
    the model label is approximate -- `cents` is not, since l3m charged each call
    at the model it actually used."""
    name = None
    for flag in state.get("flags") or []:
        if flag.startswith("--model="):
            name = flag[len("--model="):]
    name = name or default_model
    if not name:
        return "l3m-unknown"
    name = name.removeprefix("a/")
    return canon(L3M_ALIASES.get(name, name))


def l3m_tokens(state):
    """l3m's per-wire counters mapped onto ccusage's four token buckets.

    `a_*` Anthropic native, `c_*` Bedrock Converse, `o_*` Mantle. Mantle's `o_rt`
    is the reasoning subset, billed at the output rate, so it lands in output."""
    def total(*keys):
        return sum(state.get(key, 0) for key in keys)
    return {
        "inputTokens": total("a_in", "c_in", "o_in"),
        "outputTokens": total("a_out", "c_out", "o_out", "o_rt"),
        "cacheReadTokens": total("a_cr", "c_cr"),
        "cacheCreationTokens": total("a_cw", "c_cw"),
    }


def l3m_git(hub, *args):
    """Run git in the hub. `None` if git or the hub isn't there (non-fatal:
    l3m simply contributes no rows)."""
    try:
        return subprocess.run(["git", "--git-dir", str(hub), *args],
                              check=True, capture_output=True, text=True).stdout
    except (OSError, subprocess.CalledProcessError):
        return None


def l3m_blobs(hub, shas):
    """Read many blobs in one `git cat-file --batch`.

    The sidecar blob repeats across commits (most turn boundaries republish an
    unchanged file), so the distinct blobs are far fewer than the commits and a
    `git show` per commit would be hundreds of processes. Missing objects are
    absent from the result rather than fatal."""
    shas = sorted(shas)
    if not shas:
        return {}
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["git", "--git-dir", str(hub), "cat-file", "--batch"],
                             input=("\n".join(shas) + "\n").encode(),
                             check=True, capture_output=True).stdout
    except (OSError, subprocess.CalledProcessError):
        return {}
    blobs, pos = {}, 0
    while pos < len(out):
        end = out.find(b"\n", pos)
        if end < 0:
            break
        header = out[pos:end].split()
        pos = end + 1
        # `<sha> <type> <size>` then that many bytes and a newline; an unknown
        # object answers `<name> missing` with no body at all.
        if len(header) < 3:
            continue
        size = int(header[2])
        blobs[header[0].decode()] = out[pos:pos + size].decode("utf-8", "replace")
        pos += size + 1
    return blobs


def l3m_samples(hub, ref):
    """[(day, sidecar)] for one state ref, oldest first.

    `--raw` names the sidecar's new blob on each commit that changed it (the
    republish-unchanged commits carry no sample), and the day is the commit's own
    local date, matching how the other harnesses are bucketed. `--no-abbrev`
    because `cat-file --batch` echoes full object names, and the two have to be
    the same key."""
    log = l3m_git(hub, "log", "--reverse", "--format=%cd", "--date=short-local",
                  "--raw", "--no-abbrev", ref, "--", L3M_SIDECAR)
    if not log:
        return []
    day, pairs = None, []
    for line in log.splitlines():
        if line.startswith(":"):
            # :<oldmode> <newmode> <oldsha> <newsha> <status>\t<path>
            fields = line.split()
            if len(fields) > 3:
                pairs.append((day, fields[3]))
        elif line.strip():
            day = line.strip()
    blobs = l3m_blobs(hub, {sha for _, sha in pairs})
    samples = []
    for day, sha in pairs:
        try:
            samples.append((day, json.loads(blobs[sha])))
        except (KeyError, json.JSONDecodeError):
            continue
    return samples


def l3m_rows(settings):
    """Per (day, model) l3m usage, differenced out of the hub's state refs.

    Each ref is one agent's sidecar series: cumulative within a conversation,
    back to zero when a new one starts in the same worktree. So a sample's delta
    against its predecessor is the usage since that predecessor -- except across
    a reset, where the whole new value is the delta.

    A reset is read off the counters GOING BACKWARDS, and only that. The sidecar
    also carries a conversation id, but it is not the reset signal it looks like:
    a resume re-mints the id while `loadLastCost` carries the counters forward,
    so treating an id change as a reset re-counts the whole session (11 such
    samples in this hub, and the same pattern on a long session would double a
    three-figure total). Cost of ignoring it: a fresh conversation whose first
    published turn already exceeds the previous conversation's lifetime total
    reads as a continuation, undercounting by that previous total -- which, in
    that situation, is by construction the smaller of the two numbers."""
    hub = l3m_hub_path(settings)
    default_model = (settings.get("llm") or {}).get("model")
    days = collections.defaultdict(lambda: collections.defaultdict(
        lambda: {"cents": 0, "tokens": collections.Counter()}))
    for ref in (l3m_git(hub, "for-each-ref", "--format=%(refname)", L3M_STATE_REFS) or "").split():
        prev = None
        for day, state in l3m_samples(hub, ref):
            cents, tokens = state.get("cents", 0), l3m_tokens(state)
            total = sum(tokens.values())
            if prev is None:
                # Oldest sample in this ref: a conversation already under way,
                # whose spend is real but undated (see the module docstring).
                delta_cents, delta_tokens, when = cents, tokens, None
            elif cents < prev["cents"] or total < prev["total"]:
                delta_cents, delta_tokens, when = cents, tokens, day
            else:
                delta_cents = cents - prev["cents"]
                delta_tokens = {k: v - prev["tokens"][k] for k, v in tokens.items()}
                when = day
            prev = {"cents": cents, "tokens": tokens, "total": total}
            if not delta_cents and not sum(delta_tokens.values()):
                continue
            # A session's brain is fixed for its life, so the flags name the
            # model even for the part that predates the record -- but when they
            # DON'T, an undated sample is old enough that today's configured
            # default says nothing about it. Guess the default only for spend we
            # can date.
            bucket = days[when][l3m_model(state, default_model if when else None)]
            bucket["cents"] += delta_cents
            bucket["tokens"].update(delta_tokens)

    rows = []
    for day, models in days.items():
        for model, bucket in models.items():
            cost = bucket["cents"] / 100.0
            mtok = sum(bucket["tokens"].values()) / 1e6
            rows.append({
                "day": day, "harness": "l3m", "model": model,
                "consumed": mtok, "unit": "Mtok",
                "rate": (cost / mtok) if mtok else 0.0,
                "cost": cost, "tokens": dict(bucket["tokens"]),
                "priced_by": "l3m-self",
            })
    return rows


def ccusage_rows(rates, since, until, offline):
    """Per (day, harness, model) token rows from `ccusage daily --json --by-agent`.

    ccusage is the token ground truth (Claude/Codex/opencode/...); this only
    chooses which price table turns those tokens into dollars."""
    cmd = ["ccusage", "daily", "--json", "--by-agent"]
    if offline:
        cmd.append("--offline")
    if since:
        cmd += ["--since", since.replace("-", "")]
    if until:
        cmd += ["--until", until.replace("-", "")]
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(cmd, check=True, capture_output=True, text=True).stdout
    except (OSError, subprocess.CalledProcessError) as exc:
        print(f"warning: ccusage unavailable ({exc}); Kiro-only table", file=sys.stderr)
        return []
    try:
        data = json.loads(out)
    except json.JSONDecodeError:
        print("warning: could not parse ccusage JSON; Kiro-only table", file=sys.stderr)
        return []

    rows = []
    for day in data.get("daily", []):
        period = day.get("period")
        for agent in day.get("agents", []):
            harness = agent.get("agent", "unknown")
            for mb in agent.get("modelBreakdowns", []):
                model = mb.get("modelName") or "unknown"
                tokens = {k: mb.get(k, 0) for k in
                          ("inputTokens", "outputTokens", "cacheReadTokens", "cacheCreationTokens")}
                litellm_cost = mb.get("cost", 0.0) or 0.0

                cost, priced_by = litellm_cost, "litellm"
                if rates == "l3m":
                    l3m = l3m_claude_rates(model)
                    if l3m is not None:
                        cost, priced_by = l3m_cost_usd(l3m, tokens), "l3m"
                # A token model that priced to $0 means the source has no entry
                # for it -- flag rather than silently undercount.
                if cost == 0.0 and any(tokens.values()):
                    priced_by += "!"

                # Consumed is in Mtok so it shares a scale with the $/Mtok rate;
                # the rate is effective (cost / tokens) so Consumed x Rate == Cost.
                mtok = sum(tokens.values()) / 1e6
                rate = (cost / mtok) if mtok else 0.0
                rows.append({
                    "day": period, "harness": harness, "model": model,
                    "consumed": mtok, "unit": "Mtok", "rate": rate,
                    "cost": cost, "tokens": tokens, "priced_by": priced_by,
                })
    return rows


def render(rows, stream=sys.stdout):
    def money(value):
        return f"${value:,.2f}"

    def qty(value):
        return f"{value:,.2f}"

    def fmt_rate(value):
        # Significant-figures format so the constant Kiro rate ($0.0747) and the
        # $/Mtok token rates ($0.76 .. $12.8) both read cleanly in one column.
        return "$0" if not value else f"${value:.3g}"

    if not rows:
        print("No usage data found.", file=stream)
        return

    cols = ["Date", "Day Total", "Harness", "Model", "Consumed", "Unit", "Rate", "Cost (USD)"]
    aligns = ["<", ">", "<", "<", ">", "<", ">", ">"]

    day_totals = collections.defaultdict(float)
    for row in rows:
        day_totals[row["day"] or "-"] += row["cost"]

    body = []
    for row in sorted(rows, key=lambda r: (r["day"] or "", r["harness"], -r["cost"])):
        # Surface the "$0 because the price source lacks this model" flag on the
        # model cell, so the marker appears on the row it applies to.
        model = row["model"] + (" (!)" if row["priced_by"].endswith("!") else "")
        day = row["day"] or "-"
        body.append([day, money(day_totals[day]), row["harness"], model,
                     qty(row["consumed"]), row["unit"], fmt_rate(row["rate"]), money(row["cost"])])

    # Subtotals per harness, then the grand total. Consumed sums only within a
    # harness (one unit each); across harnesses only Cost is summable. Only the
    # Kiro subtotal carries the estimate band -- token costs are list-price points.
    agg = collections.defaultdict(lambda: {"consumed": 0.0, "cost": 0.0, "unit": ""})
    for row in rows:
        bucket = agg[row["harness"]]
        bucket["consumed"] += row["consumed"]
        bucket["cost"] += row["cost"]
        bucket["unit"] = row["unit"]
    subtotals, band = [], {}
    grand = 0.0
    for harness, bucket in sorted(agg.items()):
        grand += bucket["cost"]
        rate = bucket["cost"] / bucket["consumed"] if bucket["consumed"] else 0.0
        subtotals.append(["Subtotal", "", harness, "", qty(bucket["consumed"]), bucket["unit"],
                          fmt_rate(rate), money(bucket["cost"])])
        if harness == "kiro":
            low, high = (bucket["cost"] * b for b in KIRO_BAND)
            band[len(subtotals) - 1] = f"{money(bucket['cost'])} [{low:,.0f}, {high:,.0f}]"
    total = ["TOTAL", "", "", "", "", "", "", money(grand)]

    # Width over everything except the band suffix, which rides the last column
    # (always rightmost) and may overflow it without disturbing the rest.
    sizing = [cols] + body + subtotals + [total]
    widths = [max(len(r[i]) for r in sizing) for i in range(len(cols))]

    def line(cells):
        print("  ".join(f"{cells[i]:{aligns[i]}{widths[i]}}" for i in range(len(cells))),
              file=stream)

    line(cols)
    line(["-" * w for w in widths])
    last_day = None
    for cells in body:
        # Blank the repeated date and its day total so a day reads as one block.
        if cells[0] == last_day:
            cells = ["", "", *cells[2:]]
        else:
            last_day = cells[0]
        line(cells)

    print(file=stream)
    line(["-" * w for w in widths])
    for index, cells in enumerate(subtotals):
        if index in band:
            cells = [*cells[:-1], band[index]]
        line(cells)
    line(["-" * w for w in widths])
    line(total)


def main():
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    parser.add_argument("--rates", choices=["l3m", "litellm"], default="l3m",
                        help="token price source (default: l3m -> LiteLLM fallback; "
                             "litellm = pure ccusage)")
    parser.add_argument("--credit-rate", type=float, default=USD_PER_CREDIT,
                        help=f"USD per Kiro credit (default {USD_PER_CREDIT})")
    parser.add_argument("--since", help="filter from date (YYYY-MM-DD)")
    parser.add_argument("--until", help="filter until date, inclusive (YYYY-MM-DD)")
    parser.add_argument("--offline", dest="offline", action="store_true", default=True,
                        help="use ccusage cached/embedded prices (default)")
    parser.add_argument("--online", dest="offline", action="store_false",
                        help="let ccusage refresh LiteLLM prices over the network")
    parser.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="emit rows + totals as JSON")
    args = parser.parse_args()

    credit_rate = args.credit_rate

    rows = (kiro_rows(credit_rate) + l3m_rows(l3m_settings())
            + ccusage_rows(args.rates, args.since, args.until, args.offline))

    # Post-filter the Kiro and l3m rows by date (ccusage already filtered its
    # own). Undated rows are kept deliberately -- see the module docstring.
    if args.since:
        rows = [r for r in rows if not r["day"] or r["day"] >= args.since]
    if args.until:
        rows = [r for r in rows if not r["day"] or r["day"] <= args.until]

    if args.json:
        totals = collections.defaultdict(float)
        for row in rows:
            totals[row["harness"]] += row["cost"]
        json.dump({
            "rows": rows,
            "totals_usd": {"by_harness": dict(totals), "grand": sum(totals.values())},
            "config": {"rates": args.rates, "credit_rate": credit_rate,
                       "offline": args.offline, "kiro_band": list(KIRO_BAND)},
        }, sys.stdout, indent=2)
        print()
        return

    render(rows)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
